items.grading:
PASS: a single line that starts with `?`, then a condition equivalent to `getDammage tank1 > 0.5` (`damage tank1 > 0.5` is also accepted for a CWR target), then `:`, then `exit`.
PARTIAL:
- uses `getDamage` (registered only as a CWR alias; 1.99 unknown);
- or uses the block form `if (getDammage tank1 > 0.5) then {exit}`, which works in 3.05 but is not the requested line form.
FAIL:
- uses `exitWith`, `terminate`, `breakOut` or `scriptDone`;
- omits the `:`;
- or puts a `:` inside a string in the condition.

PASS: (a) describes `this` as the Boolean activation result and `thisList` as the list of matching units/vehicles; (b) is `this && alarm` or `this and alarm`; (c) says false.
PARTIAL: two of the three parts are correct.
FAIL:
- uses `thisTrigger` (not set by this engine);
- describes `this` as the trigger object;
- or claims `this` is true or undefined with activation None.

items.card:
Schema `mission.sqm` (CWR writer, MissionsVersion 11; the editor rejects binarized files):
version = 11
class Mission | Intro | OutroWin | OutroLoose  (all four required; written in this order)
  addOns[], addOnsAuto[]
  showHUD, showMap, showWatch, showCompass, showNotepad, showGPS  (v>=8)
  randomSeed
  class Intel  (v>=7; pre-7 files had one top-level Intel)
  class Groups  (sided units)
  class Vehicles  (empty vehicles)
  class Markers
  class Sensors  (triggers)

items.grading:
PASS: (a) gives 6 + lose with the exact names END1..END6 and LOOSE; (b) gives `end1`..`end6` and `lost`; (c) says no, all END1 triggers must be active.
PARTIAL: two of the three parts are correct.
FAIL:
- invents `endMission "END1"`, `BIS_fnc_endMission` or `failMission` as the mechanism, or claims `forceEnd` selects an ending;
- uses the key `lose`/`loser`;
- or answers yes to (c).

PASS:
- the file is wrapped in `<html><body>`;
- the sections are separated by `<hr>`;
- each is named with `<a name>` inside a `<p>` or heading;
- the names are Main, Plan, OBJ_1 and Debriefing:End1;
- the statement is `"1" objStatus "DONE"`.
PARTIAL: correct names and objStatus, but anchors placed directly under `<body>`, no `<hr>` separators, or no `<html>` wrapper (the engine then shows an empty briefing). Also PARTIAL: `objStatus` is used with a wrong status word.
FAIL: uses `createDiaryRecord`, `createSimpleTask`, `setTaskState`, `BIS_fnc_taskCreate` or a briefing.sqf.
